 ## Background
-The Shear-warp algorithm was designed by Lacroute et al. in 1994 [S2, unofficial][S12]. It was recognized as the fastest software render algorithm at the time [S2, unofficial][S12]. The basic idea is to factorize the projection matrix into a 3D shear and 2D warp [S1, unofficial][S12]. Using the shearing, the data set is transformed into sheared object space where all viewing rays are parallel to one coordinate axis and the volume is considered as a stack of 2D 2D slices [S1, unofficial][S12]. The sheared object space values are composed using the sheared object space values. Finally the intermediate image is warped to the image plane [S1, unofficial][S12].
+The Shear-warp algorithm was designed by Lacroute et al. in 1994 [S2, unofficial][S12]. It was recognized as the fastest software render algorithm at the time [S2, unofficial][S12]. The basic idea is to factorize the projection matrix into a 3D shear and 2D warp [S1, unofficial][S12]. Using the shearing, the data set is transformed into sheared object space where all viewing rays are parallel to one coordinate axis and the volume is considered as a stack of 2D 2D slices [S1, unofficial][S12]. The intermediate image is then warped to the image plane [S1, unofficial][S12].
 
-The algorithm was implemented in VolumePro hardware, which was specialized for this algorithm [S2, unofficial][S12]. VolumePro was the first single-chip hardware, which is compatible with consumer PCs, for real-time volume rendering [S2, unofficial]. It was based on the Cube-4 framework [S2, unofficial]. This hardware was specialized for shear-wrap algorithm describe in [48] (Lacroute et al.) [S2, unofficial]. Instead of linear interpolation, trilinear interpolation was performed to achieve a better image quality [S2, unofficial]. Other features, such as super-sampling and cropping were also incorporated into the VolumePro's architecture [S2, unofficial]. Compare to cluster based method, the VolumePro architecture offers an affordable alternative for real-time volume rendering [S2, unofficial].
-
-The Shear-warp algorithm is a hybrid volume rendering algorithm that exhibits characteristics of both image-order and object-order algorithms [S3, unofficial]. It renders the volume onto an image plane parallel to one of the volume faces, then warps or distorts this intermediate image to generate the desired image, avoiding the computational expense of rendering volumes at arbitrary rotations [S3, unofficial]. This process is often referred to as a “shear-warp factorization of the viewing matrix” in the literature [S3, unofficial].
-
-The Shear-warp algorithm was proposed to avoid the problems of image-order algorithms (which visit voxels many times) and object-order algorithms (which could not perform early ray termination) [S3, unofficial]. It allows for early ray termination (via skipping opaque pixels), whereas splatting could not perform the ray-casting equivalent of early ray termination [S3, unofficial].
-
-The algorithm assumes the view direction vector $v_o$ is mostly parallel to the +z axis ($v_{o,z} > v_{o,x}$ and $v_{o,z} > v_{o,y}$) to define shear slopes [S7, unofficial]. If the view is along x or y (or negative x or y), the voxel coordinates must be reordered by transposing the coordinate axes [S3, unofficial]. To avoid re-ordering voxels when view direction changes, three encoded RLE volumes are required, one for each main viewing axis [S3, unofficial].
-
-For parallel projection, every voxel slice has the same scale factor, which can be chosen arbitrarily (e.g., unity) to create a one-to-one mapping between voxels and intermediate-image pixels [S3, unofficial]. The warping step later handles arbitrary image sizes [S3, unofficial]. True sampling rate in z varies between [1.0, 1.72] due to shearing [S3, unofficial]. Thus Nyquist theorem is almost always violated, leading to staircasing artifacts for diagonal views (e.g., at 45°) [S3, unofficial]. Blurring occurs for magnified views because the volume is pre-shaded [S3, unofficial]. If the opacity transfer function changes, the RLE volume must be re-encoded, making it not good for interactive iso-surface modification [S3, unofficial].
-
-Shear-warp uses 2D rather than 3D filters for resampling, making it 1st order in the plane of the slice but 0-order between slices, which can cause issues with high frequencies perpendicular to slices [S4, unofficial].
+The algorithm has been implemented in various forms. It was implemented in VolumePro hardware, which was specialized for this algorithm [S2, unofficial][S12]. VolumePro was the first single-chip hardware compatible with consumer PCs for real-time volume rendering [S2, unofficial]. A GPU-based implementation of the Shear-Warp algorithm was claimed to be the first implementation on the GPU, providing real-time frame rates and outperforming CPU-based implementations [S7, unofficial].
 
